+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the
+data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`. Roles:
+
+- `viewer`: reads only (`GET`).
+- `cook`: reads, and `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key gets 401 `unauthorized`; a
+known key without permission gets 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request other than `GET` made with a known key, whatever its outcome,
+adds an audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`.
+`GET /audit` lists them newest first (managers only). Keys themselves are
+never listed.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
